ion, and then in 1960, when it became the independent state of Mali. The colony was formally called French Sudan from 1890 until 1899 and then again from 1921 until 1958, and had a variety of different names over the course of its existence. The colony was initially established largely as a military project led by French troops, but in the mid-1890s it came under civilian administration.\nA number of administrative reorganizations in the early 1900s brought increasing French administration over issues like agriculture, religion, and slavery."},{"qid":"Q1049","from_t":1956,"to_t":2020,"method":"name-label+date","confidence":0.95,"label":"Sudan","description":"country in Northeast Africa","inception":1956,"dissolved":null,"enwiki":"Sudan","summary":"Sudan, officially the Republic of the Sudan, is a country in Northeast Africa. It borders the Central African Republic to the southwest, Chad to the west, Libya to the northwest, Egypt to the north, the Red Sea to the east, Eritrea and Ethiopia to the southeast, and South Sudan to the south. Sudan has a population of 51.8 million people as of 2025 and occupies 1,886,068 square kilometres (728,215 square miles), making it Africa's third-largest country by area. Sudan's capital and most populous city is Khartoum."}],"facts":[{"qid":"Q508014","kind":"capital","value_qid":"Q3703","value_label":"Bamako","from_t":1899,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P36","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Bamako"},{"qid":"Q508014","kind":"official_language","value_qid":"Q150","value_label":"French","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P37","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"French"},{"qid":"Q508014","kind":"language","value_qid":"Q150","value_label":"French","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P2936","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"French"},{"qid":"Q508014","kind":"predecessor","value_qid":"Q3090194","value_label":"Khasso","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P1365","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Khasso"},{